  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -473,18 +473,25 @@ the string, including the terminating null.\n The buffer is allocated in the given wmem scope (see README.wmem for more\n information).\n \n-int tvb_get_nstringz(tvbuff_t *tvb, const int offset, const unsigned bufsize, uint8_t* buffer);\n-int tvb_get_nstringz0(tvbuff_t *tvb, const int offset, const unsigned bufsize, uint8_t* buffer);\n+int tvb_get_raw_bytes_as_stringz(tvbuff_t *tvb, const int offset, const unsigned bufsize, uint8_t* buffer);\n \n-Copies bufsize bytes, including the terminating NULL, to buffer. If a NULL\n+Copies up to bufsize - 1 bytes to buffer and adds a terminating NUL. If a NUL\n terminator is found before reaching bufsize, only the bytes up to and including\n-the NULL are copied. Returns the number of bytes copied (not including\n-terminating NULL), or -1 if the string was truncated in the buffer due to\n-not having reached the terminating NULL. In this case, the resulting\n-buffer is not NULL-terminated.\n-tvb_get_nstringz0() works like tvb_get_nstringz(), but never returns -1 since\n-the string is guaranteed to have a terminating NULL. If the string was truncated\n-when copied into buffer, a NULL is placed at the end of buffer to terminate it.\n+the NUL are copied. If no NUL is found, then bufsize - 1 bytes are copied and a\n+NUL byte is added to ensure null termination. If fewer bytes are available than\n+bufsize - 1, as many bytes as are present in the tvb are copied and a NUL\n+terminator is added. Bufsize must be at least 1 to allow space for the NUL.\n+Returns the number of bytes copied, not including terminating NUL.\n+\n+WARNING - This function does not do encoding validation and does not guarantee\n+that it produces a UTF-8 string, and the result should never be added to the\n+tree, columns, or other output without validation. (This might be used, for\n+example, to handle character encodings not supported by the API yet.)\n+\n+int tvb_get_raw_bytes_as_string(tvbuff_t *tvb, const int offset, const unsigned bufsize, uint8_t* buffer);\n+\n+Similar to the above, but does not stop at a NUL byte and always copies as\n+many bytes up to bufsize - 1 as possible.\n \n char *tvb_get_ts_23_038_7bits_string(wmem_allocator_t *scope, tvbuff_t *tvb,\n                                      const int bit_offset, int no_of_chars);\n",
